Let nums be a list of -1, 2, 1, and -4.
Let target be 1.
Sort nums.
Let last be the last position of nums.
Let best be 0.
Let best distance be 2147483647.
For every first from 0 to last.
Let second be one more than first.
Let third be last.
Repeat while second is less than third.
Let total be item first of nums plus item second of nums plus item third of nums.
Let difference be total minus target.
If difference is less than 0, set difference to 0 minus difference.
If difference is less than best distance, set best distance to difference, set best to total.
If total is less than target, add 1 to second.
If total is more than target, subtract 1 from third.
If total is target, add 1 to second, subtract 1 from third.

Print best.
